sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-04> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Cells join into domains that make decisions as a single unit: when left-right asymmetry is randomized in early embryos, a whole domain picks L or R identity rather than individual cells choosing independently, and in frog melanoma-like conversion all melanocytes in a body convert or not together.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cell domains make coordinated group decisions, even random ones";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Computational Boundary of a \"Self\": Developmental Bioelectricity Drives Multicellularity and Scale-Free Cognition”, Frontiers in psychology (2019), doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688; section “Body Patterning and Cognition: A Common Origin”. Scope: Left-right patterning in early vertebrate embryos; melanocyte conversion in Xenopus tadpoles"
}
