    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "Remarkably, however, this randomization is made on a group level – in each case, the entire domain randomly picks L or R identity, not exhibiting a speckled appearance where each cell adopts a stochastic outcome. The decision is random, but all of the cells in the domain are coordinated to make the same random decision (Levin et al., 2002).".
